# Clerk — the waitlist on /waitlist is the only thing on this site that uses it.
#
# A Clerk application has TWO instances, and they are not interchangeable:
#
#   Development  pk_test_… / sk_test_…   works on localhost and on preview URLs
#   Production   pk_live_… / sk_live_…   works ONLY on the domain you registered
#
# Live keys reject every other origin with:
#
#   "Invalid HTTP Origin header — the Request HTTP Origin header must be equal
#    to or a subdomain of the requesting URL." (code: origin_invalid)
#
# which is what you get if you put production keys in a local .env. It is not a
# misconfiguration of this app; the keys are doing exactly what they promise.
#
# So:
#   .env.local   -> DEVELOPMENT keys, for localhost. Gitignored.
#   Vercel env   -> PRODUCTION keys, set in the dashboard, never committed.
#
# Both are in Clerk Dashboard → API keys, with the instance switcher at the top
# of the page deciding which pair you are looking at.

NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_me
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# Also required, once, in the Clerk Dashboard:
#   Access mode -> Waitlist        (the <Waitlist /> component needs this)
#   Email       -> enabled         (so invitations can be sent)

# The holyfit API, for the catalogue console on /admin.
#
# No trailing slash; the client strips one anyway. Nothing else on this site
# talks to a backend, so leaving it unset costs the marketing pages nothing —
# /admin says in as many words that it is missing, which is the only place
# anybody can act on it.
#
#   staging      https://staging.api.useholyfit.com
#   production   https://api.useholyfit.com
#
# Point a local console at staging rather than production. Writing the
# catalogue is writing the product's own content, and there is no undo in the
# console beyond typing it again.
#
# The administrator claim is NOT configured here. It is `role: admin` in the
# Clerk account's *public* metadata, which the session token carries as
# `app_role` and the database's row-level security reads. This site cannot
# grant it and does not try to: /admin shows the form to whoever holds the
# claim, and the database refuses the write to whoever does not.
HOLYFIT_API_URL=https://staging.api.useholyfit.com
